</svg>
<div></div>
</div>

<p class="fig-cap">No threshold on x separates the classes (− in the middle, + on both sides). Add the feature x² and the horizontal line x² = 2.5 separates them.</p>

**Why the kernel is a trick.** For a = (1, 2) and b = (3, 1), the polynomial kernel is (a·b + 1)² = (3 + 2 + 1)² = **36**: one dot product and a square. The same number by building the 6-dimensional features φ(x) = (1, √2x₁, √2x₂, x₁², x₂², √2x₁x₂) and taking their dot product: 1 + 6 + 4 + 9 + 4 + 12 = **36**. The kernel gets the high-dimensional answer without ever building φ.

<!-- #endregion kernel -->
<!-- #region nb -->

Ten days: the weather, the state of the car, and whether the person went out.

| Day | Weather | Car | Decision |
|:-:|---|---|---|
| 1 | Sunny | Working | Go out |
| 2 | Rainy | Broken | Go out |
| 3 | Sunny | Working | Go out |
| 4 | Sunny | Working | Go out |
| 5 | Sunny | Working | Go out |
| 6 | Rainy | Broken | Stay home |
| 7 | Rainy | Broken | Stay home |
| 8 | Sunny | Working | Stay home |
| 9 | Sunny | Broken | Stay home |
| 10 | Rainy | Broken | Stay home |

**Step 1. Count, per class** (the "training" of Naive Bayes is just this table):

| Class | P(class) | P(Sunny ∣ c) | P(Rainy ∣ c) | P(Working ∣ c) | P(Broken ∣ c) |
|---|:-:|:-:|:-:|:-:|:-:|
| Go out | 5/10 | 4/5 | 1/5 | 4/5 | 1/5 |
| Stay home | 5/10 | 2/5 | 3/5 | 1/5 | 4/5 |

**Classify (Sunny, Working).** Go out: 5/10 × 4/5 × 4/5 = **0.32**; Stay home: 5/10 × 2/5 × 1/5 = **0.04**. → **Go out**. Normalised, P(Go out ∣ Sunny, Working) = 0.32/0.36 = 0.889.

**Classify (Rainy, Working).** Go out: 5/10 × 1/5 × 4/5 = **0.08**; Stay home: 5/10 × 3/5 × 1/5 = **0.06**. → **Go out**. Normalised, P(Go out ∣ Rainy, Working) = 0.08/0.14 = 0.571.

<!-- #endregion nb -->
<!-- #region tree -->

| # | Income | Credit | Loan approved |
|:-:|---|---|---|
| 1 | High | Good | Yes |
| 2 | High | Bad | Yes |
| 3 | High | Good | Yes |
| 4 | Low | Good | Yes |
| 5 | Low | Bad | No |
| 6 | Low | Bad | No |
| 7 | High | Bad | No |
| 8 | Low | Good | Yes |

**Parent:** 5 Yes, 3 No. Entropy H = −(5/8)log₂(5/8) − (3/8)log₂(3/8) = **0.9544**; Gini = 1 − (5/8)² − (3/8)² = **0.4688**.

| Split on | Branches | Weighted H | Info gain | Weighted Gini | Gini decrease |
|---|---|--:|--:|--:|--:|
| Income | High: 3Y 1N (H = 0.8113, Gini = 0.375); Low: 2Y 2N (H = 1, Gini = 0.5) | 0.9056 | **0.0488** | 0.4375 | **0.0312** |
| Credit | Bad: 1Y 3N (H = 0.8113, Gini = 0.375); Good: 4Y 0N (H = 0, Gini = 0) | 0.4056 | **0.5488** | 0.1875 | **0.2812** |

**Credit wins on both measures.** Its Good branch is pure (4 Yes, 0 No), so it becomes a leaf at once. The Bad branch (rows 2, 5, 6, 7: 1 Yes, 3 No) is split again on Income: Low → No (2 of 2), High → mixed (1 Yes, 1 No: a leaf by majority, or a tie to report).

<!-- #endregion tree -->
<!-- #region golftree -->

